{
  "sn12.66:0.1": "Linked Discourses 12.66 ",
  "sn12.66:0.2": "7. The Great Chapter ",
  "sn12.66:0.3": "Probing Within ",
  "sn12.66:1.1": "So I have heard. ",
  "sn12.66:1.2": "At one time the Buddha was staying in the land of the Kurus, near the Kuru town named Kammāsadamma. ",
  "sn12.66:1.3": "There the Buddha addressed the mendicants, ",
  "sn12.66:1.4": "“Mendicants!” ",
  "sn12.66:1.5": "“Venerable sir,” they replied. ",
  "sn12.66:1.6": "The Buddha said this: ",
  "sn12.66:1.7": "“Mendicants, do you probe within?” ",
  "sn12.66:1.8": "When he said this, one of the mendicants said to the Buddha, ",
  "sn12.66:1.9": "“Sir, I probe within.” ",
  "sn12.66:1.10": "“But mendicant, how do you probe within?” ",
  "sn12.66:1.11": "Then that mendicant answered, ",
  "sn12.66:1.12": "but the Buddha was not happy with the answer. ",
  "sn12.66:2.1": "When he had spoken, Venerable Ānanda said to the Buddha, ",
  "sn12.66:2.2": "“Now is the time, Blessed One! Now is the time, Holy One! ",
  "sn12.66:2.3": "Let the Buddha speak of probing within. The mendicants will listen and remember it.” ",
  "sn12.66:2.4": "“Well then, Ānanda, listen and apply your mind well, I will speak.” ",
  "sn12.66:2.5": "“Yes, sir,” they replied. ",
  "sn12.66:2.6": "The Buddha said this: ",
  "sn12.66:3.1": "“Take a mendicant who probes within: ",
  "sn12.66:3.2": "‘The suffering that arises in the world starting with old age and death takes many and diverse forms. ",
  "sn12.66:3.3": "But what is 